      "rev_n_1_8fb9ab_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_8fb9ab_0",
        "node_id": "n_1_8fb9ab",
        "thought_text": "Check if the current hand already contains a mentsu (koutsu or shuntsu). If yes, the answer is 0.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794553896.1035407
      },
      "rev_n_2_f99f23_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_f99f23_0",
        "node_id": "n_2_f99f23",
        "thought_text": "If no mentsu exists, check if adding one tile can form a mentsu. This happens if two tiles are identical (need 1 more for koutsu) or two tiles are consecutive in the same suit (need 1 more for shuntsu). If yes, the answer is 1.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794553896.1035643
      },
      "rev_n_3_b8bf17_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_b8bf17_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_b8bf17",
        "thought_text": "If neither of the above conditions is met, it is always possible to form a mentsu by drawing two specific tiles (e.g., to complete a triplet or a sequence from scratch). Thus, the answer is 2.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794553896.1035786
      },
      "rev_n_2_f99f23_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_f99f23_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_f99f23",
        "thought_text": "The error occurs because the code only checks for two consecutive tiles to form a sequence, missing the case where two tiles are separated by exactly one number (e.g., 4p and 2p can form a sequence with 3p). The corrected reasoning must also check if any two tiles in the same suit have a difference of 2, as adding the missing middle tile creates a valid shuntsu.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_f99f23_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_a93291d362",
        "created_at": 1794553928.9457154
      },
      "rev_n_4_6dbe19_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_6dbe19_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_6dbe19",
        "thought_text": "Check if the hand already forms a mentsu (koutsu or shuntsu). If so, output 0.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "4397370732467052103",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794553957.4320512
      },
      "rev_n_5_cf57af_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_cf57af_0",
        "node_id": "n_5_cf57af",
        "thought_text": "If no mentsu exists, check if adding one tile can form a mentsu by looking for pairs or near-sequences. If possible, output 1.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "4397370732467052103",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794553957.4320853
      },
      "rev_n_6_23ed51_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_6_23ed51_0",
        "node_id": "n_6_23ed51",
        "thought_text": "If neither 0 nor 1 is possible, the answer must be 2, as any two additional tiles can always complete a triplet or sequence from the remaining single tile or by forming a new pair.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "4397370732467052103",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794553957.4320989
      },
      "rev_n_7_71766b_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_7_71766b_0",
        "node_id": "n_7_71766b",
        "thought_text": "Check if the hand already contains a mentsu (koutsu or shuntsu); if so, the answer is 0. Otherwise, check if adding one tile can form a mentsu by looking for pairs with difference 0 (for koutsu) or difference 1 or 2 (for shuntsu) in the same suit.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "6588189219218767907",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794553974.0257554
      },
      "rev_n_8_a24a7d_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_8_a24a7d_0",
        "node_id": "n_8_a24a7d",
        "thought_text": "If no mentsu exists with 0 or 1 draws, verify if 2 draws are sufficient. Since any two tiles of the same suit can form a sequence with at most 2 additional tiles (e.g., 1 and 9 need 2, 3 and 5 need 1), and any single tile can form a triplet with 2 more, the maximum answer is always 2 unless it's already 0 or 1.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "6588189219218767907",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794553974.025774
      },
      "rev_n_9_c793a6_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_9_c793a6_0",
        "node_id": "n_9_c793a6",
        "thought_text": "Implement a systematic check: parse the input into (number, suit) tuples, group by suit, then for each group check all pairs for potential koutsu (diff=0) or shuntsu (diff=1 or 2). If found, return 1. If the initial check found a mentsu, return 0. Else return 2.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "6588189219218767907",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794553974.0257857
      },
