      "rev_n_16_032a7f_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_16_032a7f_0",
        "node_id": "n_16_032a7f",
        "thought_text": "First, check if the current hand already contains a mentsu (triplet or sequence). If yes, output 0. Otherwise, check if adding one tile can complete a mentsu by looking for pairs with difference 0 (for triplet) or difference 1 or 2 (for sequence) in the same suit. If yes, output 1. Otherwise, output 2.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5167839031153994896",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794554111.9546447
      },
      "rev_n_17_3b4585_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_17_3b4585_0",
        "node_id": "n_17_3b4585",
        "thought_text": "Iterate through all possible pairs of tiles in the hand. For each pair in the same suit, calculate the difference in their numbers. If the difference is 0, we need 1 more tile to make a triplet. If the difference is 1 or 2, we need 1 more tile to make a sequence. If any such pair exists, the answer is 1. If no such pair exists after checking all combinations, the answer is 2.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5167839031153994896",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794554111.954668
      },
      "rev_n_18_3b9c1e_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_18_3b9c1e_0",
        "node_id": "n_18_3b9c1e",
        "thought_text": "Since the maximum answer is always 2 (we can always draw 3 identical tiles or a sequence to win), we only need to distinguish between 0, 1, and 2. Start by verifying the existence of a complete mentsu. Then verify if a partial mentsu (2 tiles) exists that can be completed with 1 draw. If neither condition is met, the answer defaults to 2.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5167839031153994896",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794554111.9546793
      },
